Bounds on an `impl` block make methods conditional, as you saw with `impl<T: PartialOrd> Pair<T>`. Bounds also let you implement a trait **for every type that implements another trait**. This is a **blanket implementation**. The standard library has this one:

```rust
impl<T: Display> ToString for T {
    // ...
}
```

That is why you can call `.to_string()` on any type that implements `Display`: integers, `char`, your own types once you implement `Display` for them.

